"The System tracks a mage's power rather than granting it, and what watches through it is unknown."
"Grounds a mage breaks alone become skills the System names later, for any who follow that path."
"A skill rebuilt to run better can evolve, shown as \"Old Name > New Name\"."
"The world has an authority, a net of gold lines of pure mana, that bars what it judges impossible."
"Filth touching the world's authority dirties it, and it recoils like tape from dust."
"A mage with a truly new path may hear \"World Acknowledges Path: <name>\", once in an age."
"Acknowledgement locks a mage onto their path, and world mana then doubles their recent gains."
"Realising a truth about the world through one's path may itself wake mana."
"A mage who climbs to Tier 4 without a path is weakened for good."
"Tier bought with herbs and potions leaves a shaky foundation that a lower Tier can exploit."
"Ascension beyond Tier 10 is held a myth; none is recorded in ten thousand years."
"Mixing curse power and mana in one channel turns it all to curse power."
"A mage's core sits behind a near-unbreakable barrier, and meddling with it can end their future."
